src-tauri/target/
*.png
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
!docs/ref-shots/**/*.png
# recon evidence for R34 (title rename): the shots ARE the measurement — a
# prose claim about a focus ring is not verifiable, the pixels are.
!docs/recon-title-rename/**/*.png
# recon evidence for scroll-sync: the shots carry the L<NNNN> markers the whole
# measurement is read from — measure.sh re-derives every number from these pngs.
!docs/recon-scroll-sync/**/*.png
dist/
.cov-evidence/

# per-worktree goal state (display, HOME, TMPDIR). Generated by scripts/wt.sh.
# NEVER tracked: a committed .goalenv merges into another goal and `cd`s it
# into the WRONG worktree — that happened 2026-09-12 (drop-attach -> main ->
# inline-title), which is how a goal ends up building in a peer's tree.
.goalenv
# recon-bmmenu: the stock 1.13.7 bookmark-row menu — the README reads every label off these
!docs/recon-bmmenu/**/*.png
# docs/palette-wasp/reference.png is the operator picture the wasp palette is traced to (criterion 1 of goal/wasp)
!docs/palette-wasp/reference.png
# recon-tabmenu: the stock 1.13.7 NOTE TAB menu. Every row count, box size and
# wording in docs/recon-tabmenu/README.md is read off these crops, so they are
# the measurement, not decoration. Without this exception the shots are silently
# ignored: iteration 3 reported "five shots committed" and `git ls-files` showed
# none — `git add` on an ignored path is a no-op that prints nothing.
!docs/recon-tabmenu/**/*.png

# recon-dotfiles: the evidence IS the deliverable — .gitignore line 2 (*.png)
# would otherwise keep every cited shot out of a clone (measured on themearch
# and on srclick: README cites a path a reviewer cannot open).
!docs/recon-dotfiles/**/*.png
# recon-srclick: acceptance criterion 1 is "every C1-C12 answer names a shot
# that EXISTS under docs/recon-srclick/shots/" — so these pngs are the evidence
# a reviewer opens, not incidental screenshots. The numbers beside them live in
# docs/recon-srclick/measurements/*.json (DOM state) and *-scroll.json (frames).
!docs/recon-srclick/**/*.png
# rvcursor: the pointer crops and masks ARE the measurement (criteria 2 and 5).
# A prose claim about a cursor shape is not verifiable; the pixels are, and the
# masks are what the classifier compares.
!docs/recon-rvcursor/**/*.png
!docs/negctl-rvcursor/**/*.png
# recon-flatpak: shots/ is the launch evidence for the goal's criterion 2 — a
# .flatpak that "launches" is a claim until the pixels are in the tree next to
# the census line that measured them (docs/recon-flatpak, item L).
!docs/recon-flatpak/**/*.png
# recon-tabclose: the S3 measurement — stock 1.13.7 ORPHANS the tab ("No file")
# on an external rename/delete instead of closing it. The title log alone cannot
# show that the tab is still in the strip; 11-ren-after.png and 21-del-after.png can.
!docs/recon-tabclose/shots/*.png
# recon-bmfolder: criterion 1 is "every answer names a committed shot it was
# read from" — group creation, the group row menu, indent geometry, delete and
# restart are all read off these pngs, so they are evidence, not screenshots.
!docs/recon-bmfolder/shots/*.png
# themecsp: the egress-proof evidence (shots ARE the deliverable, criterion 1-2)
!docs/themecsp/**/*.png

# recon-bmcompat: stock 1.13.7's OWN bookmarks.json is the spec for goal
# bmcompat, and every claim in docs/recon-bmcompat/README.md names the shot it
# was read from — line 2 (*.png) would drop exactly the evidence, so unignore
# it here. The .bookmarks.json captures under captures/ are not ignored.
!docs/recon-bmcompat/**/*.png
# recon-navbtn: stock 1.13.7 back/forward nav buttons — every geometry px,
# icon and disabled-state claim in docs/recon-navbtn/README.md is read off
# these shots, so they are the measurement, not decoration.
!docs/recon-navbtn/**/*.png

# fixtures/themefs: the two shots ARE the fixture's provenance — stock 1.13.7's
# own UI saying "Minimal INSTALLED/ACTIVE" and the Appearance pane showing the
# dropdown on Minimal with "1 theme installed". Without this exception line 2
# (*.png) silently drops exactly the evidence the fixture README cites.
!docs/fixtures/themefs/shots/*.png

# fixtures/themeone: same reason, for the Solarized fixture criterion 4 needs —
# stock 1.13.7's own community browser saying "Solarized INSTALLED / ACTIVE"
# with its whole UI repainted, and the filter showing "Showing 1 theme", which
# is what makes "installed via stock's OWN installer" checkable instead of
# claimed.
!docs/fixtures/themeone/shots/*.png

# recon-bmdrag: criterion 1 is "every claim names a committed shot" — the drop
# indicator's position, thickness and colour are read off these pngs.
!docs/recon-bmdrag/shots/*.png

# recon-themes: T9 (the graph's background) is measured BY PIXEL — the four
# sentinel counts in README.md's T9 ANSWER are re-derived from these pngs, so
# the shots ARE the measurement. T1-T8's shots and logs were force-added
# file-by-file with no rule, which is why T9's were silently dropped by line 2
# on the first `git add -A docs/` (it printed nothing, exactly the failure the
# recon-tabmenu comment above records). Rule, not a habit:
!docs/recon-themes/**/*.png
# ...and the probe transcripts every number is grepped out of. `logs` is
# excluded repo-locally in .git/info/exclude (which cannot be committed, by
# design); a .gitignore negation outranks info/exclude, and the DIRECTORY has
# to be re-included or git never descends into it to see the files.
!docs/recon-themes/**/logs/
!docs/recon-themes/**/logs/*.log

# recon-bmcollapse: criterion 2 is "every shot the README cites exists under
# docs/recon-bmcollapse/shots/ and is NOT git-ignored" — line 2 (*.png) would
# drop exactly the evidence for where stock keeps a collapsed group, what the
# pane-header toggle does and what is at the bottom edge of the sidebar.
!docs/recon-bmcollapse/shots/*.png

# recon-sidefont: criterion 1 is "every Q1-Q5 answer cites a committed shot and
# `git check-ignore -v` over shots/ prints nothing" — the font px, row pitch and
# baselines are read off these pngs, and ours-before/after.png are criterion 6.
!docs/recon-sidefont/shots/*.png

# recon-lgpanes: criterion 1 is "every Q1-Q6 answer cites a committed shot" and
# criterion 5 puts ours-before/ours-after.png here — the right-pane contents
# (kept / followed / empty) are read off these pngs, so they are the evidence.
!docs/recon-lgpanes/shots/*.png

# recon-listtoggle: Q1 (palette names, Hotkeys "Blank" rows, the ids bound on
# disk), Q9's frontmatter selection and Q14's "No commands found" are read off
# these shots — line 2 (*.png) would drop exactly the cited evidence.
!docs/recon-listtoggle/shots/*.png
# recon-setcenter: the stock 1.13.7 settings modal geometry (Q1-Q4) and ours-before/after —
# the README cites these shots as the evidence; without this they would be silently ignored.
!docs/recon-setcenter/**/*.png
# recon-rvtask: stock 1.13.7 reading-view task clicks; the README cites every shot, and ours-before/ours-after (A5) live beside them
!docs/recon-rvtask/**/*.png
# recon-collapseall: criterion A1 is "README answers Q1-Q5 citing committed
# shots, git check-ignore -v over shots prints nothing" and A4 puts the
# ours-after shots in the same directory — line 2 (*.png) would drop both.
!docs/recon-collapseall/shots/*.png
# recon-overlaytheme: every Q1-Q6 answer and every R1 table row cites one of
# these shots (the sentinel frames ARE the measurement); without this exception
# `git add` silently drops them.
!docs/recon-overlaytheme/**/*.png
